>> thank you, MADAM Clerk.

00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:19.714
Hello, mayor.

00:06:19.714 --> 00:06:20.150
thank you for being here,

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:22.150
mayor.

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.589
In 2014 our city made a promise

00:06:28.589 --> 00:06:29.557
to end traffic deaths by 2024.

00:06:29.557 --> 00:06:32.293
It was an initiative that was

00:06:32.293 --> 00:06:32.928
spearheaded by my predecessor,

00:06:32.928 --> 00:06:34.928
district seven supervisor

00:06:35.664 --> 00:06:36.640
norman yee also PRESIDENT Of

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.640
the board.

00:06:39.601 --> 00:06:40.302
He himself was a victim, a

00:06:40.302 --> 00:06:42.702
survivor of traffic violence

00:06:43.671 --> 00:06:44.105
which left him disabled for

00:06:44.105 --> 00:06:46.105
almost a year.

00:06:46.874 --> 00:06:47.175
He had to learn how to walk

00:06:47.175 --> 00:06:47.976
again.

00:06:47.976 --> 00:06:50.546
His wife who was a teacher who

00:06:50.546 --> 00:06:51.313
was a teacher at the time had

00:06:51.313 --> 00:06:51.747
to take time off of work to

00:06:51.747 --> 00:06:53.747
care for him.

00:06:55.284 --> 00:06:57.284
>> unfortunate early this

00:06:58.454 --> 00:06:59.521
promise in our actions leading

00:06:59.521 --> 00:07:02.190
up to it or after it have not

00:07:02.190 --> 00:07:02.590
really yielded the results that

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:04.590
we intended.

00:07:06.361 --> 00:07:06.995
The this last year we saw 39

00:07:06.995 --> 00:07:09.395
people lose their lives

00:07:10.466 --> 00:07:11.200
and many more injuries.

00:07:11.200 --> 00:07:14.470
These deaths and the tens of

00:07:14.470 --> 00:07:15.204
thousands of additional crashes

00:07:15.204 --> 00:07:17.672
that took place on our streets

00:07:17.672 --> 00:07:18.240
have cost san francisco

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.240
billions of dollars.

00:07:21.977 --> 00:07:25.448
Last week we you know, had a

00:07:25.448 --> 00:07:26.150
rally where we talked about a

00:07:26.150 --> 00:07:28.150
budget and legislative

00:07:29.351 --> 00:07:31.751
analyst's report that estimated

00:07:32.188 --> 00:07:32.788
the costs at $2.5 billion over

00:07:32.788 --> 00:07:33.589
the last five years.

00:07:33.589 --> 00:07:36.589
>> and you know, our street

00:07:36.959 --> 00:07:40.229
safety budget is a very small

00:07:40.229 --> 00:07:40.563
portion of the mta budget

00:07:40.563 --> 00:07:41.296
overall.

00:07:41.296 --> 00:07:43.696
You have championed public

00:07:44.334 --> 00:07:47.334
safety and security and also

00:07:48.204 --> 00:07:48.971
economic recovery on our

00:07:48.971 --> 00:07:49.572
streets and this is very much

00:07:49.572 --> 00:07:51.972
part of public safety.

00:07:52.541 --> 00:07:56.141
So today my question is what

00:07:56.412 --> 00:07:57.213
commitments and investments do

00:07:57.213 --> 00:08:00.750
you intend to make in order to

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:01.351
renew our goal of zero deaths

00:08:01.351 --> 00:08:03.751
and establish the next

00:08:04.421 --> 00:08:04.854
iteration of a vision zero

00:08:04.854 --> 00:08:05.288
policy for us?

00:08:05.288 --> 00:08:07.288
>> thank you.

00:08:08.240 --> 00:08:08.991
Supervisor.

00:08:08.991 --> 00:08:11.894
As I said a minute ago, public

00:08:11.894 --> 00:08:12.628
safety is my top priority and I

00:08:12.628 --> 00:08:15.280
appreciate the opportunity to

00:08:15.131 --> 00:08:15.865
partner with many of you

00:08:15.865 --> 00:08:18.769
in this room on that work.

00:08:18.769 --> 00:08:19.503
And I want to be crystal clear

00:08:19.503 --> 00:08:22.472
I believe that traffic safety

00:08:22.472 --> 00:08:23.340
is public safety.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:23.907
I want san franciscans to feel

00:08:23.907 --> 00:08:26.307
safe on our streets.

00:08:27.610 --> 00:08:28.440
That means feeling safe from

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.440
any threat.

00:08:30.313 --> 00:08:30.980
But when we talk about vision

00:08:30.980 --> 00:08:31.681
zero zero, we're not just

00:08:31.681 --> 00:08:33.850
talking about traffic safety.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:34.617
We're talking about the kind of

00:08:34.617 --> 00:08:35.419
city that we want to be.

00:08:35.419 --> 00:08:37.821
From day one my administration

00:08:37.821 --> 00:08:38.455
has focused on restoring safety

00:08:38.455 --> 00:08:38.822
and accountability in san

00:08:38.822 --> 00:08:40.822
francisco.

00:08:41.925 --> 00:08:42.592
And I believe they're at the

00:08:42.592 --> 00:08:44.895
core of making our streets

00:08:44.895 --> 00:08:45.629
safer for everyone.

00:08:45.629 --> 00:08:48.290
Let's start with enforcement.

00:08:48.631 --> 00:08:49.366
You've heard the public, you've

00:08:49.366 --> 00:08:52.536
seen the data and when people

00:08:52.536 --> 00:08:53.137
engage in reckless driving flee

00:08:53.137 --> 00:08:55.537
from law enforcement or

00:08:55.806 --> 00:08:56.473
endanger lies behind the wheel

00:08:56.473 --> 00:08:56.873
,they must be held

00:08:56.873 --> 00:08:58.873
accountable.

00:08:59.743 --> 00:09:00.444
That's how we restore order

00:09:00.444 --> 00:09:01.144
and protect our communities.

00:09:01.144 --> 00:09:04.414
And I believe we need more

00:09:04.414 --> 00:09:05.148
officers on our streets to

00:09:05.148 --> 00:09:08.418
enforce the rules of the road

00:09:08.418 --> 00:09:09.190
because traffic laws only work

00:09:09.190 --> 00:09:11.190
when they're enforced.

00:09:12.123 --> 00:09:12.857
Supervisor mandel hearings made

00:09:12.857 --> 00:09:13.524
that clear and that's why many

00:09:13.524 --> 00:09:14.158
of us stood together this

00:09:14.158 --> 00:09:16.558
