02:11:13.473 --> 02:11:16.277
funds from a wide range of

02:11:16.277 --> 02:11:16.944
local parks and open space

02:11:16.944 --> 02:11:18.944
organizations according to

02:11:20.213 --> 02:11:20.982
recent new reports.

02:11:20.982 --> 02:11:24.184
It appears that these funds MAY

02:11:24.184 --> 02:11:24.918
have been siphoned off to pay

02:11:24.918 --> 02:11:27.318
for parks alliance's operating

02:11:28.688 --> 02:11:29.323
costs in violation of their

02:11:29.323 --> 02:11:31.323
fiduciary and contractual

02:11:32.692 --> 02:11:33.528
duties to these organizations.

02:11:33.528 --> 02:11:35.963
The parks alliance, whose long

02:11:35.963 --> 02:11:36.730
term excessive executive

02:11:36.730 --> 02:11:39.730
director recently left has been

02:11:39.767 --> 02:11:40.401
slow in being forthright with

02:11:40.401 --> 02:11:42.401
these organizations city

02:11:43.804 --> 02:11:44.738
agencies and the public.

02:11:44.738 --> 02:11:47.908
>> so it is time to use this

02:11:47.908 --> 02:11:48.575
board's powers of inquiry

02:11:48.575 --> 02:11:50.975
including if necessary our

02:11:51.579 --> 02:11:52.313
subpoena powers.

02:11:52.313 --> 02:11:55.830
It has been widely reported

02:11:55.830 --> 02:11:55.917
that the parks alliance, which

02:11:55.917 --> 02:11:58.285
serves as a fiscal sponsor for

02:11:58.285 --> 02:11:58.886
some 80 neighborhood based

02:11:58.886 --> 02:12:01.286
friends of local park

02:12:01.655 --> 02:12:03.655
organizations including a

02:12:04.792 --> 02:12:05.459
number in district ten has been

02:12:05.459 --> 02:12:07.859
unable to timely reimburse

02:12:08.696 --> 02:12:09.464
these organizations for funds

02:12:09.464 --> 02:12:12.333
that they hold on their behalf.

02:12:12.333 --> 02:12:13.670
>> I am also deeply troubled by

02:12:13.670 --> 02:12:15.937
the fact that there are city

02:12:15.937 --> 02:12:16.604
departments including the port

02:12:16.604 --> 02:12:19.740
of san francisco and our rec

02:12:19.740 --> 02:12:20.308
and parks department that MAY

02:12:20.308 --> 02:12:22.308
be negatively impact.

02:12:24.278 --> 02:12:24.979
I need to remind all of us that

02:12:24.979 --> 02:12:27.379
our concerns regarding the

02:12:28.383 --> 02:12:29.117
parks alliance go back at least

02:12:29.117 --> 02:12:32.117
five years after they were

02:12:32.554 --> 02:12:34.823
implicated in a scandal for

02:12:34.823 --> 02:12:35.423
taking almost $1 million from

02:12:35.423 --> 02:12:37.823
recology in exchange for

02:12:37.992 --> 02:12:38.693
favorable garbage rates.

02:12:38.693 --> 02:12:41.930
Subsequently this board held

02:12:42.263 --> 02:12:42.630
hearings about the parks

02:12:42.630 --> 02:12:44.630
alliance.

02:12:45.934 --> 02:12:46.635
In 2021 I raised specific

02:12:46.635 --> 02:12:49.350
concerns regarding the port's

02:12:49.538 --> 02:12:50.238
request to enter into an mou

02:12:50.238 --> 02:12:53.238
and accept and expand grants.

02:12:53.808 --> 02:12:54.442
Ultimately in 2022 the board

02:12:54.442 --> 02:12:56.842
approved this request to

02:12:57.845 --> 02:13:00.245
receive 3.25 million in grant

02:13:01.884 --> 02:13:02.417
funds for crane cove park for

02:13:02.417 --> 02:13:03.180
the parks alliance.

02:13:03.180 --> 02:13:05.418
After we insisted on

02:13:05.621 --> 02:13:06.454
significant changes

02:13:06.454 --> 02:13:09.691
and safeguards thus far it is

02:13:09.691 --> 02:13:12.460
my understanding that the port

02:13:12.460 --> 02:13:14.860
has received $975,000 of these

02:13:16.130 --> 02:13:16.931
funds and it is unclear if the

02:13:16.931 --> 02:13:17.599
parks alliance will be able to

02:13:17.599 --> 02:13:20.690
provide the balance of the

02:13:20.690 --> 02:13:21.700
funds owed.

02:13:21.700 --> 02:13:24.340
Also I was shocked to find out

02:13:24.340 --> 02:13:25.410
that after our approvals the

02:13:25.410 --> 02:13:28.443
port did not end up entering

02:13:28.443 --> 02:13:28.944
into the mou that this board

02:13:28.944 --> 02:13:30.944
approved in 2023.

02:13:31.980 --> 02:13:32.614
This board approved grant

02:13:32.614 --> 02:13:34.916
agreement with the parks

02:13:34.916 --> 02:13:35.651
alliance for $2 million to

02:13:35.651 --> 02:13:38.510
benefit india basin shoreline

02:13:38.754 --> 02:13:39.488
park in my district.

02:13:39.488 --> 02:13:42.525
It is unclear whether we have

02:13:42.525 --> 02:13:43.159
received the benefits provided

02:13:43.159 --> 02:13:45.559
for under that agreement

02:13:46.495 --> 02:13:47.162
and there are numerous other

02:13:47.162 --> 02:13:49.998
agreements rec and park has

02:13:49.998 --> 02:13:50.966
with the parks alliance.

02:13:50.966 --> 02:13:51.533
We need to know the status of

02:13:51.533 --> 02:13:53.933
all of these grants.

02:13:54.504 --> 02:13:57.440
Last week parks alliance made

02:13:57.440 --> 02:13:58.740
conflicting statements to the

02:13:58.740 --> 02:14:00.474
press regarding what has

02:14:01.176 --> 02:14:01.877
transpired a parks alliance

02:14:01.877 --> 02:14:04.446
board member was quoted as

02:14:04.446 --> 02:14:05.147
saying they had not spent the

02:14:05.147 --> 02:14:05.814
restricted funds but was then

02:14:05.814 --> 02:14:08.214
contradicted by their board

02:14:08.850 --> 02:14:09.118
PRESIDENT Who said that they

02:14:09.118 --> 02:14:09.818
had.

02:14:09.818 --> 02:14:12.818
We need a full financial

02:14:12.822 --> 02:14:13.590
accounting from parks alliance

02:14:13.590 --> 02:14:16.892
and our city agencies as well

02:14:16.892 --> 02:14:19.862
as answers to how the city

02:14:19.862 --> 02:14:20.596
intends to recoup funds owed to

02:14:20.596 --> 02:14:21.264
us and to many of these

02:14:21.264 --> 02:14:23.664
organizations that MAY be

02:14:24.660 --> 02:14:24.733
in jeopardy.

02:14:24.733 --> 02:14:25.401
>> the rest I submit.

02:14:25.401 --> 02:14:27.801
Thank you, MR. PRESIDENT.

02:14:28.238 --> 02:14:28.638
Supervisor chan submit.

02:14:28.638 --> 02:14:30.638
Thank you.

02:14:32.208 --> 02:14:32.675
Supervisor chen submit.

02:14:32.675 --> 02:14:33.376
>> thank you.

02:14:33.376 --> 02:14:35.611
Supervisor dorsey thank you,

02:14:35.611 --> 02:14:36.279
MADAM Clerk.

02:14:36.279 --> 02:14:38.279
>> colleagues with today's

02:14:38.848 --> 02:14:39.549
final passage of the recovery

02:14:39.549 --> 02:14:42.451
first ordinance I am calling

02:14:42.451 --> 02:14:43.152
for a hearing to solicit input

02:14:43.152 --> 02:14:45.552
from relative relevant city

02:14:46.323 --> 02:14:47.900
agencies for possible revisions

02:14:47.900 --> 02:14:49.490
to the 2021 ordinance mandating

02:14:50.260 --> 02:14:50.994
annual reports on overdose

02:14:50.994 --> 02:14:53.394
prevention policies with long

02:14:54.230 --> 02:14:54.698
term recovery from substance

02:14:54.698 --> 02:14:55.432
use disorders.

02:14:55.432 --> 02:14:58.534
Poised to be enshrined as the

02:14:58.534 --> 02:14:58.934
primary goal of san francisco's

02:14:58.934 --> 02:15:00.934
drug policy.

02:15:02.472 --> 02:15:03.140
I hope to hear from department

02:15:03.140 --> 02:15:03.874
heads and drug treatment

02:15:03.874 --> 02:15:06.677
professionals on how we might

02:15:06.677 --> 02:15:07.377
best update and expand upon

02:15:07.377 --> 02:15:09.777
this annual reporting mandate

02:15:10.280 --> 02:15:11.140
so that moving forward will

02:15:11.140 --> 02:15:13.140
receive departmental recovery

02:15:13.950 --> 02:15:14.351
and overdose prevention reports

02:15:14.351 --> 02:15:15.118
every year.

02:15:15.118 --> 02:15:17.518
Agencies currently required to

02:15:17.854 --> 02:15:18.555
report under this law are the

02:15:18.555 --> 02:15:19.322
department of public health,

02:15:19.322 --> 02:15:21.722
the department of homelessness

02:15:22.920 --> 02:15:22.860
and supportive housing.

02:15:22.860 --> 02:15:23.527
h soc which is the healthy

02:15:23.527 --> 02:15:24.194
streets operations center

02:15:24.194 --> 02:15:26.263
through the department of

02:15:26.263 --> 02:15:26.864
emergency management and the

02:15:26.864 --> 02:15:28.864
human services agency.

02:15:30.167 --> 02:15:30.901
Currently these annual reports

02:15:30.901 --> 02:15:33.670
generally serve to inform us

02:15:33.670 --> 02:15:34.371
about how our city agencies

02:15:34.371 --> 02:15:36.771
together with their nonprofit

02:15:37.573 --> 02:15:38.309
contractors offer services to

02:15:38.309 --> 02:15:38.976
people who use drugs to help

02:15:38.976 --> 02:15:41.512
them use drugs more safely

02:15:41.512 --> 02:15:42.146
and to help reduce overdoses.

02:15:42.146 --> 02:15:44.146
Now obviously overdose

02:15:46.216 --> 02:15:46.917
prevention is necessary but not

02:15:46.917 --> 02:15:47.384
sufficient for us as a drug

02:15:47.384 --> 02:15:49.384
policy strategy.

02:15:50.687 --> 02:15:51.421
One thing I think everyone seem

02:15:51.421 --> 02:15:52.956
to agree on in the debate

02:15:52.956 --> 02:15:53.690
around recovery first was that

02:15:53.690 --> 02:15:56.461
drug recovery and drug use for

02:15:56.461 --> 02:15:57.228
that matter aren't linear

02:15:57.228 --> 02:16:00.665
and that there is no one size

02:16:00.665 --> 02:16:01.465
fits all approach.

02:16:01.465 --> 02:16:02.233
This hearing on how we best

02:16:02.233 --> 02:16:04.633
implement recovery and overdose

02:16:04.668 --> 02:16:05.335
prevention policies will

02:16:05.335 --> 02:16:08.335
reflect the truth that not

02:16:08.839 --> 02:16:09.573
every person who uses drugs

02:16:09.573 --> 02:16:12.443
wants to keep using drugs

02:16:12.443 --> 02:16:13.111
in perpetuity for those who do.

02:16:13.111 --> 02:16:15.947
Yes of course we should

02:16:15.947 --> 02:16:16.714
encourage harm reduction

02:16:16.714 --> 02:16:17.115
practices to use deadly drugs

02:16:17.115 --> 02:16:19.115
more safely.

02:16:19.383 --> 02:16:20.840
But for the many san

02:16:20.840 --> 02:16:20.785
franciscans struggling with

02:16:20.785 --> 02:16:23.185
substance use disorders who

02:16:23.688 --> 02:16:24.422
want to be in recovery or who

02:16:24.422 --> 02:16:27.422
aspire to live a self-directed

02:16:27.491 --> 02:16:28.159
and healthy life free from

02:16:28.159 --> 02:16:31.159
illicit drug use as our

02:16:31.295 --> 02:16:32.264
recovery first policy reflects

02:16:32.264 --> 02:16:32.864
,it only makes sense that we

02:16:32.864 --> 02:16:35.233
should hear from city

02:16:35.233 --> 02:16:35.967
departments on what roles they

02:16:35.967 --> 02:16:36.267
can play to help accomplish

02:16:36.267 --> 02:16:38.267
that.

02:16:39.304 --> 02:16:39.904
This hearing on recovery

02:16:39.904 --> 02:16:40.638
and overdose prevention

02:16:40.638 --> 02:16:42.773
policies is an important step

02:16:42.773 --> 02:16:43.541
forward in that regard.

02:16:43.541 --> 02:16:46.577
I want to thank mayor larry's

02:16:46.577 --> 02:16:47.177
team and his department heads

02:16:47.177 --> 02:16:47.946
for their openness to

02:16:47.946 --> 02:16:50.415
collaborating on this and other

02:16:50.415 --> 02:16:51.116
steps to elevate long term

02:16:51.116 --> 02:16:54.850
recovery in our drug policy

02:16:54.850 --> 02:16:54.819
approach.

02:16:54.819 --> 02:16:55.353
Thanks as well to colleagues

02:16:55.353 --> 02:16:57.353
PRESIDENT Randleman

02:16:58.423 --> 02:16:59.900
in particular is joining me as

02:16:59.900 --> 02:17:02.900
a hearing co-sponsor and I

02:17:02.930 --> 02:17:02.794
certainly welcome others.

02:17:02.794 --> 02:17:03.528
Mostly, however, I want to

02:17:03.528 --> 02:17:05.531
thank those in san francisco's

02:17:05.531 --> 02:17:06.365
recovery community.

02:17:06.365 --> 02:17:09.365
I am continually inspired by

02:17:09.968 --> 02:17:10.669
those who have been showing up

02:17:10.669 --> 02:17:13.438
and speaking out in increasing

02:17:13.438 --> 02:17:14.306
numbers not to criticize or

02:17:14.306 --> 02:17:17.475
condemn but to ask for a role

02:17:17.475 --> 02:17:17.775
to play in the drug crisis we

02:17:17.775 --> 02:17:19.775
face.

02:17:20.578 --> 02:17:21.346
I saw it just last night with

02:17:21.346 --> 02:17:22.800
dozens of people who showed up

02:17:22.800 --> 02:17:24.383
for a community meeting at the

02:17:24.383 --> 02:17:25.184
queen hotel in my neighborhood.

02:17:25.184 --> 02:17:28.530
The queen will be a first of

02:17:28.530 --> 02:17:28.720
its kind recovery oriented

02:17:28.720 --> 02:17:31.120
health respite facility for

02:17:31.624 --> 02:17:32.324
unhoused adults fighting to get

02:17:32.324 --> 02:17:35.460
and to stay clean and sober.

02:17:35.460 --> 02:17:36.940
It is moving to see so many

02:17:36.940 --> 02:17:38.940
recovery community members

02:17:39.664 --> 02:17:40.433
willing to help others who face

02:17:40.433 --> 02:17:43.433
challenges similar to those we

02:17:43.469 --> 02:17:44.136
have faced to carry the message

02:17:44.136 --> 02:17:46.772
that grappling with a drug

02:17:46.772 --> 02:17:47.606
addiction need not condemn

02:17:47.606 --> 02:17:50.576
anyone to a lifetime of drug

02:17:50.576 --> 02:17:51.276
use and to bear witness to the

02:17:51.276 --> 02:17:54.790
truth that the promise of

02:17:54.790 --> 02:17:54.846
recovery for a better,

02:17:54.846 --> 02:17:57.846
healthier life free of illicit

02:17:58.170 --> 02:17:58.718
drug use is possible for every

02:17:58.718 --> 02:17:59.318
san franciscan who wants it

02:17:59.318 --> 02:18:01.854
and the rest I submit.

02:18:01.854 --> 02:18:02.421
>> thank you supervisor dorsey

02:18:02.421 --> 02:18:04.421
supervisor and gaudio.

02:18:05.624 --> 02:18:06.325
submit.

